H2700.definition:
from H2691 (חָצֵר) and H4194 (מָוֶת); village of death;
Chatsarmaveth, a place in Arabia
KJV: Hazarmaveth.

H2701.definition:
from H2691 (חָצֵר) and H5484 (סוּסָה); village of cavalry;
Chatsar-Susah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Hazar-susah.

H2702.definition:
from H2691 (חָצֵר) and the plural of H5483 (סוּס); village of horses;
Chatsar-Susim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Hazar-susim.

H2703.definition:
from H2691 (חָצֵר) and a derivative of H5869 (עַיִן); village of springs;
Chatsar-Enon, a place in Palestine
KJV: Hazar-enon.

H2704.definition:
from H2691 (חָצֵר) and the same as H5881 (עֵינָן); village of springs;
Chatsar-Enan, a place in Palestine
KJV: Hazar-enan.

H2705.definition:
from H2691 (חָצֵר) and H7776 (שׁוּעָל); village of (the) fox;
Chatsar-Shual, a place in Palestine
KJV: Hazar-shual.

H2706.definition:
from H2710 (חָקַק);
an enactment; hence, an appointment (of time, space, quantity, labor or usage)
KJV: appointed, bound, commandment, convenient, custom, decree(-d), due, law, measure, [idiom] necessary, ordinance(-nary), portion, set time, statute, task.

H2707.definition:
a primitive root;
to carve; by implication, to delineate; also to entrench
KJV: carved work, portrayed, set a print.

H2708.definition:
feminine of H2706 (חֹק), and meaning substantially the same
{an enactment; hence, an appointment (of time, space, quantity, labor or usage)}
KJV: appointed, custom, manner, ordinance, site, statute.

H2709.definition:
from an unused root probably meaning to bend; crooked;
Chakupha, one of the Nethinim
KJV: Hakupha.

H2710.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to hack, i.e. engrave (Judges 5:14, to be a scribe simply); by implication, to enact (laws being cut in stone or metal tablets in primitive times) or (gen.) prescribe
KJV: appoint, decree, governor, grave, lawgiver, note, pourtray, print, set.

H2711.definition:
from H2710 (חָקַק);
an enactment, a resolution
KJV: decree, thought.

H2712.definition:
or (fully) חוּקֹק; from H2710 (חָקַק); appointed;
Chukkok or Chukok, a place in Palestine
KJV: Hukkok, Hukok.

H2713.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to penetrate; hence, to examine intimately
KJV: find out, (make) search (out), seek (out), sound, try.

H2714.definition:
from H2713 (חָקַר);
examination, enumeration, deliberation
KJV: finding out, number, (un-) search(-able, -ed, out, -ing).

H2716.definition:
from an unused (and vulgar) root probably meaning to evacuate the bowels;
excrement
KJV: dung. Also חֲרִי.

H2717.definition:
or חֲרֵב; a primitive root;
to parch (through drought) i.e. (by analogy,) to desolate, destroy, kill
KJV: decay, (be) desolate, destroy(-er), (be) dry (up), slay, [idiom] surely, (lay, lie, make) waste.

H2718.definition:
(Aramaic) a root corresponding to H2717 (חָרַב);
to demolish
KJV: destroy.

H2719.definition:
from H2717 (חָרַב);
drought; also a cutting instrument (from its destructive effect), as a knife, sword, or other sharp implement
KJV: axe, dagger, knife, mattock, sword, tool.

H2720.definition:
from H2717 (חָרַב);
parched or ruined
KJV: desolate, dry, waste.

H2721.definition:
a collaterally form of H2719 (חֶרֶב);
drought or desolation
KJV: desolation, drought, dry, heat, [idiom] utterly, waste.

H2722.definition:
from H2717 (חָרַב); desolate;
Choreb, a (generic) name for the Sinaitic mountains
KJV: Horeb.

H2723.definition:
feminine of H2721 (חֹרֶב);
properly, drought, i.e. (by implication) a desolation
KJV: decayed place, desolate (place, -tion), destruction, (laid) waste (place).

H2724.definition:
feminine of H2720 (חָרֵב);
a desert
KJV: dry (ground, land).

H2725.definition:
from H2717 (חָרַב);
parching heat
KJV: drought.

H2726.definition:
or חַרְבוֹנָה; of Persian origin;
Charbona or Charbonah, a eunuch of Xerxes
KJV: Harbona, Harbonah.

H2727.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to leap suddenly, i.e. (by implication) to be dismayed
KJV: be afraid.

H2728.definition:
from H2727 (חָרַג);
the leaping insect, i.e. a locust
KJV: beetle.

H2729.definition:
a primitive root;
to shudder with terror; hence, to fear; also to hasten (with anxiety)
KJV: be (make) afraid, be careful, discomfit, fray (away), quake, tremble.

H2730.definition:
from H2729 (חָרַד);
fearful; also reverential
KJV: afraid, trembling.

H2731.definition:
feminine of H2730 (חָרֵד);
fear, anxiety
KJV: care, [idiom] exceedingly, fear, quaking, trembling.

H2732.definition:
the same as H2731 (חֲרָדָה);
Charadah, a place in the Desert
KJV: Haradah.

H2733.definition:
patrial from a derivative of H2729 (חָרַד) (compare H5878 (עֵין חֲרֹד));
a Charodite, or inhabitant of Charod
KJV: Harodite.

H2734.definition:
a primitive root (compare H2787 (חָרַר));
to glow or grow warm; figuratively (usually) to blaze up, of anger, zeal, jealousy
KJV: be angry, burn, be displeased, [idiom] earnestly, fret self, grieve, be (wax) hot, be incensed, kindle, [idiom] very, be wroth. See H8474 (תַּחָרָה).

H2735.definition:
from H2356 (חוֹר) and a collateral (masculine) form of H1412 (גֻּדְגֹּדָה), with the article interposed; hole of the cleft;
Chor-hag-Gidgad, a place in the Desert
KJV: Hor-hagidgad.

H2736.definition:
; from H2734 (חָרָה) and H3050 (יָהּ); fearing Jah;
Charhajah, an Israelite
KJV: Harhaiah.

H2737.definition:
from an unused root meaning to perforate;
properly, pierced, i.e. a bead of pearl, gems or jewels (as strung)
KJV: chain.

H2738.definition:
or (shortened) חָרֻל; apparently, a passive participle of an unused root probably meaning to be prickly;
properly, pointed, i.e. a bramble or other thorny weed
KJV: nettle.

H2739.definition:
from passive participle of H2763 (חָרַם) and H639 (אַף); snub-nosed;
Charumaph, an Israelite
KJV: Harumaph.

H2740.definition:
or (shortened) חָרֹן; from H2734 (חָרָה);
a burning of anger
KJV: sore displeasure, fierce(-ness), fury, (fierce) wrath(-ful).

H2741.definition:
a patrial from (probably) a collateral form of H2756 (חָרִיף);
a Charuphite or inhabitant of Charuph (or Chariph)
KJV: Haruphite.

H2742.definition:
or חָרֻץ; passive participle of H2782 (חָרַץ);
properly, incised or (active) incisive; hence (as noun masculine or feminine) a trench (as dug), gold (as mined), a threshing-sledge (having sharp teeth); (figuratively) determination; also eager
KJV: decision, diligent, (fine) gold, pointed things, sharp, threshing instrument, wall.

H2743.definition:
the same as H2742 (חֲרוּץ); earnest;
Charuts, an Israelite
KJV: Haruz.

H2744.definition:
a fuller form of H2746 (חַרְחֻר); inflammation;
Charchur, one of the Nethinim
KJV: Harhur.

H2745.definition:
from the same as H2775 (חֶרֶס); perhaps shining;
Charchas, an Israelite
KJV: Harhas.

H2746.definition:
from H2787 (חָרַר);
fever (as hot)
KJV: extreme burning.

H2747.definition:
from a primitive root meaning to engrave;
a chisel or graver; also a style forwriting
KJV: graving tool, pen.

H2748.definition:
from the same as H2747 (חֶרֶט);
a horoscopist (as drawing magical lines or circles)
KJV: magician.

H2749.definition:
(Aramaic) the same as H2748 (חַרְטֹם)
{a horoscopist (as drawing magical lines or circles)}
KJV: magician.

H2750.definition:
from H2734 (חָרָה);
a burning (i.e. intense) anger
KJV: fierce, [idiom] great, heat.

H2751.definition:
from the same as H2353 (חוּר);
white bread
KJV: white.

H2752.definition:
from H2356 (חוֹר); cave-dweller or troglodyte;
a Chorite or aboriginal Idumaean
KJV: Horims, Horites.

H2753.definition:
or חוֹרִי; the same as H2752 (חֹרִי);
Chori, the name of two men
KJV: Hori.

H2754.definition:
or חָרִט; from the same as H2747 (חֶרֶט);
properly, cut out (or hollow), i.e. (by implication) a pocket
KJV: bag, crisping pin.

H2755.definition:
from the plural of H2716 (חֶרֶא) and the plural of H3123 (יוֹנָה); or perhaps rather the plural of a single word חֲרָאיוֹן, probably a kind of vegetable
excrements of doves {or a vegetable}
KJV: doves' dung.

H2756.definition:
from H2778 (חָרַף); autumnal;
Chariph, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Hariph.

H2758.definition:
from H2790 (חָרַשׁ);
ploughing or its season
KJV: earing (time), ground.

H2759.definition:
from H2790 (חָרַשׁ) in the sense of silence;
quiet, i.e. sultry (as feminine noun, the sirocco or hot east wind)
KJV: vehement.

H2760.definition:
a primitive root;
to braid (i.e. to entangle or snare) or catch (game) in anet
KJV: roast.

H2761.definition:
(Aramaic) a root probably allied to the equivalent of H2787 (חָרַר);
to scorch
KJV: singe.

H2762.definition:
from H2760 (חָרַךְ);
properly, a net, i.e. (by analogy) lattice
KJV: lattice.

H2763.definition:
a primitive root;
to seclude; specifically (by a ban) to devote to religious uses (especially destruction); physical and reflexive, to be blunt as to the nose
KJV: make accursed, consecrate, (utterly) destroy, devote, forfeit, have a flat nose, utterly (slay, make away).

H2764.definition:
or (Zechariah 14:11) חֶרֶם; from H2763 (חָרַם);
physical (as shutting in) a net (either literally or figuratively); usually a doomed object; abstractly extermination
KJV: (ac-) curse(-d, -d thing), dedicated thing, things which should have been utterly destroyed, (appointed to) utter destruction, devoted (thing), net.

H2765.definition:
from H2763 (חָרַם); devoted;
Chorem, a place in Palestine
KJV: Horem.

H2766.definition:
from H2763 (חָרַם); snub-nosed;
Charim, an Israelite
KJV: Harim.

H2767.definition:
from H2763 (חָרַם); devoted;
Chormah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Hormah.

H2768.definition:
from H2763 (חָרַם); abrupt;
Chermon, a mount of Palestine
KJV: Hermon.

H2769.definition:
plural of H2768 (חֶרְמוֹן);
Hermons, i.e. its peaks
KJV: the Hermonites.

H2770.definition:
from H2763 (חָרַם);
a sickle (as cutting)
KJV: sickle.

H2771.definition:
from H2787 (חָרַר); parched;
Charan, the name of a man and also of a place
KJV: Haran.

H2772.definition:
patrial from H2773 (חֹרֹנַיִם);
a Choronite or inhabitant of Choronaim
KJV: Horonite.

H2773.definition:
dual of a derivative from H2356 (חוֹר); double cave-town;
Choronajim, a place in Moab
KJV: Horonaim.

H2774.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Charnepher, an Israelite
KJV: Harnepher.

H2776.definition:
the same as H2775 (חֶרֶס); shining;
Cheres, a mountain in Palestine
KJV: Heres.

H2777.definition:
from H2775 (חֶרֶס) (apparently in the sense of a red tile used for scraping);
a potsherd, i.e. (by implication) a pottery; the name of a gate at Jerusalem
KJV: east.

H2779.definition:
from H2778 (חָרַף);
properly, the crop gathered, i.e. (by implication) the autumn (and winter) season; figuratively, ripeness of age
KJV: cold, winter (-house), youth.

H2780.definition:
from H2778 (חָרַף); reproachful;
Chareph, an Israelite
KJV: Hareph.

H2781.definition:
from H2778 (חָרַף);
contumely, disgrace, the pudenda
KJV: rebuke, reproach(-fully), shame.

H2782.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to point sharply, i.e. (literally) to wound; figuratively, to be alert, to decide
KJV: bestir self, decide, decree, determine, maim, move.

H2783.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H2782 (חָרַץ) in the sense of vigor;
the loin (as the seat of strength)
KJV: loin.

H2784.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
a fetter; figuratively, a pain
KJV: band.

H2785.definition:
from H2782 (חָרַץ);
a sour grape (as sharp in taste)
KJV: kernel.

H2786.definition:
a primitive root;
to grate the teeth
KJV: gnash.

H2787.definition:
a primitive root;
to glow, i.e. literally (to melt, burn, dry up) or figuratively (to show or incite passion)
KJV: be angry, burn, dry, kindle.

H2788.definition:
from H2787 (חָרַר);
arid
KJV: parched place.

H2789.definition:
a collateral form mediating between H2775 (חֶרֶס) and H2791 (חֶרֶשׁ);
a piece of pottery
KJV: earth(-en), (pot-) sherd, [phrase] stone.

H2790.definition:
a primitive root;
to scratch, i.e. (by implication) to engrave, plough; hence (from the use of tools) to fabricate (of any material); figuratively, to devise (in a bad sense); hence (from the idea of secrecy) to be silent, to let alone; hence (by implication) to be deaf (as an accompaniment of dumbness)
KJV: [idiom] altogether, cease, conceal, be deaf, devise, ear, graven, imagine, leave off speaking, hold peace, plow(-er, man), be quiet, rest, practise secretly, keep silence, be silent, speak not a word, be still, hold tongue, worker.

H2791.definition:
from H2790 (חָרַשׁ);
magical craft; also silence
KJV: cunning, secretly.

H2793.definition:
from H2790 (חָרַשׁ);
a forest (perhaps as furnishing the material for fabric)
KJV: bough, forest, shroud, wood.

H2794.definition:
active participle of H2790 (חָרַשׁ);
a fabricator or mechanic
KJV: artificer.

H2795.definition:
from H2790 (חָרַשׁ);
deaf (whether literally or spiritual)
KJV: deaf.

H2796.definition:
from H2790 (חָרַשׁ);
a fabricator or any material
KJV: artificer, ([phrase]) carpenter, craftsman, engraver, maker, [phrase] mason, skilful, ([phrase]) smith, worker, workman, such as wrought.

H2797.definition:
from H2792 (חֶרֶשׁ); magician;
Charsha, one of the Nethinim
KJV: Harsha.

H2798.definition:
plural of H2796 (חָרָשׁ);
mechanics, the name of a valley in Jerusalem
KJV: Charashim, craftsmen.

H2799.definition:
from H2790 (חָרַשׁ);
mechanical work
KJV: carving, cutting.
